WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:12.870
If you had to invest YOUR Money in another
country, I’m sure Venezuela wouldn’t even

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.050
be on the list, right?

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:19.900
Well, friends here at VisualPolitik, China’s
Government doesn’t agree with you…

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:27.779
“China agrees to invest $20bn in Venezuela
to help offset effects of oil price slump”

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:31.190
But hold on just a second because this is
not only about China.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.330
Have you ever heard of Goldman Sachs?

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:37.489
One of those banks that symbolizes American
capitalism at its purest form?

00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:42.989
Well… they too saw a lot of business opportunities
in Maduro’s Venezuela.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:50.079
“Goldman Buys $2.8 Billion Worth of Venezuelan
Bonds, and an Uproar Begins”

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:51.530
Yep, you heard that right.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:56.230
While Venezuela is having one of the worst
economic catastrophes humanity has ever witnessed,

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.960
they keep making deals with the world’s
biggest investors.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:05.129
This is why, despite the scarcity, the extreme
poverty, and the hyperinflation, Nicolas Maduro

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:09.880
is buying state of the art weapons to maintain
an army almost nobody could attack.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:14.110
An army that has over 5000 rockets manufactured
in Russia.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:21.049
In October this year, 2017, Maduro met Vladimir
Putin again to buy weapons.

00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:27.630
Meanwhile, Venezuela is the biggest partner
China has in the region.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:32.650
They have received way more Chinese money
than any other Latin American country.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.870
So now you might wonder…

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.030
What’s the point of all of this?

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.119
Finance wise, China is blind to ideology.

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:42.140
And the same goes with the American banks.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.270
Their only goal is to make money.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:51.990
But, at a first sight, Venezuela doesn’t
look like a good place to do business.

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.700
So How come did Venezuela come to the attention
of so many investors?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.220
Where is the deal here?

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:02.030
Well, today we are going answer to all of
those questions but before we do, let’s

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:06.360
take a look back at history.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.360
A RISKY BET

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.990
Here is some advice.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:12.610
If you ever want to become a dictator in your
country, and repress your opponent and torture

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.370
your political foes, there is something you
need…

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.590
MONEY!

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:23.150
Yes, normal citizens can die from starvation
but your police and your army cannot miss

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:24.909
any pay day.

00:02:24.909 --> 00:02:31.500
The biggest problem for an authoritarian leader
like Nicolas Maduro, the Venezuelan president,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.340
is if the army strikes against him.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:42.730
But, if you’ve been following VisualPolitik
for a long time, you know that Venezuela has

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.280
almost no private companies.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.690
So there is not so much money to be collected
in taxes here.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:53.069
Further, oil exports are no longer profitable
since the oil prices went down in 2012.

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:57.550
In other words, his only way to pay for all
this repressive apparatus is by getting loans

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:04.120
on the international market.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.129
But hold on just a second because things are
not as easy as they seem!

00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:10.739
Venezuela is a country with a terrible economic
problems.

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:15.290
This means, if you lend them money, chances
are they will never give it back.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:20.360
This is why we say Venezuelan bonds are a
high risk investment.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.360
And what do countries do when investors don’t
trust them?

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.430
Well, they raise the interest rate!

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:31.000
And this is why Venezuelan bonds have a yield
of over 10 and 12% while a German bond, which

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.989
is way more reliable, doesn’t surpass the
0.5%.

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:36.500
OK, but what does this mean?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:42.099
Well, let’s imagine we invest 1000 USD in
Venezuelan bonds to be paid in 10 years with

00:03:42.099 --> 00:03:43.530
an interest of 10%.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:47.489
Theoretically, the Venezuelan government is
expected to gives us back those 1000 USD we

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:48.489
lent them.

00:03:48.489 --> 00:03:52.319
But, in the meantime, we will receive 100
dollars every year as an interest payment.

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:53.319
Oh yes!

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:54.319
I know what you are thinking!

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:56.310
This is a great business right?

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:03.540
Well, don’t get to excited yet.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:07.230
As we said before, Venezuela has a pretty
high chance to default.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:11.870
If the Government of Caracas, the capital
of Venezuela, declares bankruptcy in, say,

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.239
two years, we will have lost 80% of our investment.

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:19.720
This is why, despite the high interest rates,
Nicolas Maduro has found it harder and harder

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.769
to sell his bonds.

00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:25.840
And this explains news like this:

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:31.180
Goldman Sachs’ Venezuela bond purchase sparks
anger

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:36.800
It paid about $865m for $2.8bn worth of bonds.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.940
OK, OK, but… what does this mean?

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.580
Well, it means Goldman Sachs bought Venezuelan
bonds for a third of their value.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.840
In other words…

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.460
Theoretically, the government of Venezuela
is expected to pay back 2.8 Billion USD to

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:55.580
Goldman Sachs despite the fact they paid only
865 million USD.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.380
And why does Venezuela accept this deal?

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.600
Well, first they need cash as soon as possible.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:09.000
Second, they know they will never pay it back…

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.680
So now you might wonder…

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.699
Why do bankers lend them money if everyone
knows Venezuela won’t pay back?

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:19.170
Where is the business appeal here?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.020
So, it is in the interest rates.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:26.460
Think about it… if Venezuela gives Goldman
Sachs 10% of those 2.8 billion every year,

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.440
it means the bank will have covered their
real investment, those 865 million USD, in

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.030
less than 3 years.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.430
After that, everything is profit.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:43.600
So, of course, investors know Venezuela is
going to default.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.639
The question here is WHEN are they gonna do
it?

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:48.810
So investors are making a high risk bet here.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.030
If Venezuela keeps paying for, at least, 4
years, banks will win.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.840
If they don’t, banks will lose.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.310
And the truth is Nicolas Maduro is the first
one interested in not declaring bankruptcy...

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:02.500
On one hand, he needs to keep bankers on his
side so he can pay his repression machinery,

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:15.030
and on the other hand, PDVSA, Venezuela’s
state oil company has several properties abroad.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.350
Factories and refineries in countries like
Haiti and the Dominican Republic.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.980
If Caracas defaults, some of those investors
might seize them.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.630
This is why, for several years, Venezuela
has prioritized their debt payments over anything

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.630
else.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:32.610
Maduro’s foreign currency reserves went
from more than $50 billion to less than 10

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:33.610
billion.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:40.410
And this explains why a magazine like FORBES
said this about Venezuelan bonds in 2016.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:46.350
“Venezuela might be the worst country in
Latin America but its Bonds look great.”

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:51.310
In the middle of 2017, Donald Trump had to
pass a law banning American banks and hedge

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.009
funds from investing in Venezuela...

00:06:54.009 --> 00:07:01.350
Nonetheless, no matter how badly Maduro tried,
his economy was weaker than he thought...

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:05.580
“Venezuela to restructure foreign debt,
default looms as possibility.”

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.130
Yes, you heard that right.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:11.500
Goldman Sachs and the rest of those hedge
funds who bought Venezuelan bonds at a discount

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.500
price…

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.500
they have lost their bet.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.039
Nonetheless, there is still one investor that
is far from being worried.

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:21.700
Yes, of course we are talking about CHINA.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.919
CHINA’S PUPPET

00:07:24.919 --> 00:07:29.520
As we said at the beginning, Venezuela is
the country that received the most Chinese

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.060
money in Latin America.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:37.000
But, unlike the private bankers, China’s
government does not buy bonds on the market.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.169
Instead, Xi Jimping had a personal meeting
with Nicolas Maduro.

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:44.370
A meeting where they negotiated a special
deal.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:48.900
A loan that is not to be paid back with money,
but with oil.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:53.580
This way, Beijing makes sure they have an
oil supplier no matter what happens.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:57.080
But hold on just a second because this formula
has its drawbacks too..

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.919
As you know, PDVSA is a hyper bureaucratic
company, with thousands of workers hired by

00:08:01.919 --> 00:08:03.700
Chavez out of pure nepotism.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:11.520
This means, oil drilling is harder and harder
for them.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.889
In fact, lately, those dinosaur juice shipments
are arriving late to China.

00:08:16.889 --> 00:08:22.380
But despite all of that, China keeps their
loyalty to Venezuela…

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:27.949
”We are showing solidarity with the Venezuelan
people because we are supporting the principles

00:08:27.949 --> 00:08:29.600
of United Nations.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:33.020
This is what we have to do”

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.450
So the question is Why?

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:40.380
What does China get from Venezuela now that
they are facing problems with their oil payments?

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.360
The answer lies in the long run.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:46.390
Just think about it: Beijing has already lent
$50 billion to Caracas.

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.290
Now they just need patience.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.290
And stability...

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:53.660
Maduro need some more years to pay back his
debt?

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:54.660
No rush!

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:55.660
Xi Jimping can wait!

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:59.340
However, there is something that could risk
the payback of these debts.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:01.670
And that is a change in government.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:04.950
What would happen if the opposition to Nicolas
Maduro took power?

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:08.930
Would they be that willing to meet their obligations
to those who helped the dictator?

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:11.720
The one who sent them to jail and tortured
them?

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.240
Mmmm… that sounds ‘risky’, doesn’t
it?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:18.930
And ‘risk’ is the least favourite word
for the Chinese communist party.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:20.940
And it explains things like this one...

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:30.210
“Venezuela defends purchase of Chinese riot-control
gear after more than 70 deaths in street protests.”

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:35.890
China has already sold over 350 million dollars
worth weapons to Maduro so he can stay in

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:36.890
power.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:40.330
Thanks to these movements, Caracas is China’s
biggest ally in the region.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:45.180
Basically, the Venezuelan government is to
become the puppet of the Chinese communist

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.180
party.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.590
So, what happens?

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:51.820
Maybe China want to build new infrastructures
in South America so they can complete their

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.029
‘silk road’ project?

00:09:53.029 --> 00:09:54.240
Well, no problem!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.700
Venezuelan diplomats will support them with
no questions asked.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.339
Does China want to have a military base in
the region?

00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:00.770
Welcome to Venezuela!

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:05.540
Just like that, thousands of square miles
to place your army as you please!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.540
In other words…

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:11.780
there is no better ally than the one that
needs you in order to survive…

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:17.360
“Venezuela hopes no country hinders China's
'fantastic' Silk Road initiative.”

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:22.260
Nonetheless, there is still doubt here…
having as much power as they have, China might

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.990
request other kinds of reforms.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:28.570
For instance, if Venezuela keeps facing problems
with their oil payments, they might force

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:32.830
Maduro to fire people at PDVSA and make it
more productive.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:37.620
They could even take over the exploitation
of the oil.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:41.029
So here it is the question…

00:10:41.029 --> 00:10:43.650
Can Venezuela become China’s colony?

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:47.030
Do you think China is going to seize Venezuelan
oil for ever?

